{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bob has a number of pencils. When Bob splits them into groups of 10, he has 3 left over. When he splits them into groups of 12, he has 5 left over. Find the smallest number of pencils Bob can have.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Lists.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Lists)\">Solution 1 (Lists)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Lists)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the condition, possible numbers of pencils Bob could have are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8391cea57837e04a1cf6e1624681ddc07cb27ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3,13,23,33,43,\\boxed{53},63,\\ldots\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"23\" /> and from the second condition we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b45ab2052187236ce1e7489dd696465bcb4d56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5,17,29,41,\\boxed{53},65,\\ldots.\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"23\" /> So, the smallest number of pencils Bob could have is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1833e57ba1442553d09fae41034c95c8f4b80e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of pencils that Bob has. Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a> from the given information, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d877a9084b9956f206834b0fc9013d71ce962b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 3 \\pmod {10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235a8df667d6bdcc60966d11aa207d20c03ab162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 5 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From the first one, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/0990a2f59c47dc1579f2d3f9c870462c297e256e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10k + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> for some non-negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e453300226b9efe91689fa1c02b647f2308d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10k + 3 \\equiv 5 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43d422c6cc582d928d968c83b7da1aa72ffbabf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10k \\equiv 2 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d434d928d4b520a7c06aa2084754089f6f0bb5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2k \\equiv 2 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f70bac103aecf678fbfae0449d47d15c5b3c9b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k \\equiv -2 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a36bdae8216b8f0c335984771720a508b9b5ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\equiv 5 \\pmod {12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />, so the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa5318831f3c515c56ec2ffc74a327515dd9c0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 5 + 3 = 50 + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1833e57ba1442553d09fae41034c95c8f4b80e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024347\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 68/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3315/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31912:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024347 and revision id 291189. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}